                <pb facs="0792" n="672" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg672"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.01 Foreign Control/53: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Vice Consul at Monrovia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wall</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-02-15T08:00:00-00:44">February 15, 1931—8
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:30 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>22. Attorney General Grimes, designated to collaborate with Sottile at Geneva on
                    slavery matters, sailed on S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Sultan</hi> of the
                    German-African Line February 14th.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wall</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
